{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/882644-so-who-s-played-ran-the-streetfighter-storyteller-game","id":882644,"title":"So, who's played/Ran the Streetfighter storyteller game?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-05T00:46:50-07:00","id":882644,"title":"So, who's played/Ran the Streetfighter storyteller game?","content":"Back when this came out i was all stoked for it, but t seems to be MORE focused just for the combat angle, rather than actual proper campaign like play. However, i DID get rather into it after i got all the books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T03:04:17-07:00","id":882715,"title":"","content":"It's a rpg based off of a fighting game, what did you expect?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T13:30:40-07:00","id":883170,"title":"","content":"NB: It's actually Streetfighter the Storytelli<b>ng</b> game, not the Storytell<b>er</b> game. Hilariously, it even has some of the truncated combat steps that CoD uses, like rolling Strength + Ability to just get to the damage and dispensing with the &quot;hit, did no damage&quot; condition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T09:01:41-07:00","id":884667,"title":"","content":"I love Street Fighter and consider it part of my World of Darkness headcanon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T14:17:27-07:00","id":884897,"title":"","content":"From the additions SF had, i loved the idea on cyborgs and animal hybreds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T14:36:33-07:00","id":884915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>garhkal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/882644-so-who-s-played-ran-the-streetfighter-storyteller-game?p=884897#post884897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From the additions SF had, i loved the idea on cyborgs and animal hybreds.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could have used some better forethought on mechanics, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T11:32:47-07:00","id":885520,"title":"","content":"Much agreed there. <br /> For the fighting styles, which was your fave(s) to use?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-21T01:04:46-07:00","id":895373,"title":"","content":"I never ran a SF-only game, but I did incorporate SF characters and mechanics into a pair of &quot;rainbow Chronicles&quot; (any splat allowed, fun synergies and inter-splat exploits for all) that I ran concurrently in the mid-to-late '90s. Neither Chronicle featured SF player characters, but there were Streetfighter NPCs in both. The results weren't bad at all, and they added a splash of color to both games overall.<br /> <br /> The first Chronicle had them only as an interesting variant. While on the run from Sabbat packs hunting them in San Diego, the Kindred PCs managed to rendezvous with their Eshu ally (being in the right place at the right time is sort of the Eshu's <i>thing</i>, after all), who brought them to the toughest local joint he knew: A Changeling Freehold in the form of a punk/goth dance club and bar, run mainly by Redcaps and Sluagh. Since the vampires risked being returned to the club's mundane Seeming (thus making them detectable by the roving Sabbat hunting packs) if they stood apart from the narrative of the Freehold, they were forced to wholeheartedly indulge in a series of drinking contests, tale-telling competitions, and eventually, a stage-diving challenge. After some creative Discipline usage, the final round consisted of the Gangrel (diving into an Earth Meld is fairly impressive), the Ananasi (whose player was late to the session, and whose arachnid forms and Gifts were quite the crowd pleasers), and...NPC Streetfighter and painted-faced sumotori, E. Honda (who got seriously drunk after an earlier bout in Tijuana, and wound up in Feytown). Despite the Werespider's run-up-the-wall, spring-off-the-ceiling, land-as-ten-thousand-tiny-parachuting-spiders final\u00e9 (which was a huge hit with the Sluagh), it was Honda, and his massive Butt-Stomp leap, to Flying Head Ram torpedo, to Hundred-Hand Slap (used to high-five every single audience member before landing on the ground) that took the day. When the PCs were bounced from the Wyld shortly before dawn, they wound up having to engage with the most dogged (and toughest) Sabbat pack in a brief, but brutal firefight. It was Honda's help that tipped the scales. And though I had expected the SF NPC to fall be slaughtered in the firefight, he actually acquitted himself well, despite having only human-level Attributes and no special physical resistance. <br /> <br /> The other Chronicle put SF's mechanics much more onto center stage, as the girlfriend of the party leader &quot;came out&quot; as a Streetfighter. She occasionally fought alongside her Ventrue bf and the rest of the PCs (an Assamite, a 1st ed. Mummy, an Orphan Mage, a Fianna, and a Ferryman in training), and held her own via textbook Shotokan Karate. Of course, she had limited resistance to mindgames like Presence, Dominate, the Mind Sphere, etc. But in a square fight, even with bullets, Klaives, and Etheric Electro-Rectifiers flashing about, she was always more of an asset than a liability. Her statblock evolved to be slightly less buffed than Ken or Ryu as statted out in the SF core book, but <b>Hadoukens</b> and <b>Flaming Shoryuken</b> punches were vital to her effectiveness. <br /> <br /> Late in the campaign, the PCs took out a Tzimisce Blood Cult masquerading as a trendy Yoga studio in Beverly Hills, and she started learning Kabaddi. <b>Regeneration</b> gave her serious durability in group combat (when the large # of combatants allows allies to provide covering fire for the few moments it takes to regain lost Health levels. <b>Ghost Form</b> was the last Technique she learned, and everybody in the party wished they could learn it (including, ironically, the Wraith), as it proved to be a game-changer in melee combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1536-39steps","name":"39Steps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1536_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}